	(text "INPUT PROTECTION (record section 3). Self-acting: nothing depends on firmware or a rail it protects. LTC4364-1\n  datasheet Figure 1 topology.\nF1 Nano2 453 15 A soldered: dead-short backstop. D801 SMBJ45CA (bidirectional: survives a reversed supply)\n  clamps the hot-plug ring.\nQ1 hot-swap FET on HGATE, Q2 ideal-diode FET on DGATE, common SOURCE: reverse polarity AND reverse current\n  blocked, so the regen clamp may sit at 44.7 V.\nR1 2 mOhm CSS2H, pseudo-Kelvin (SENSE and OUT on the inner-edge sense pads): 50 mV = 25 A limit (25 mV = 12.5\n  A folded back into a short). C802 100n: ~1 ms in a dead short (36 V x 12.5 A = 450 W in Q1), ~11 ms on a\n  mild overload.\nC801 22n on HGATE: ~40 ms power-up ramp, ~0.4 A inrush into ~470 uF: the current limit and timer never engage\n  at start.\nR805/R806 402k/10k: output clamp 51.5 V, ABOVE the 44.7 V regen clamp so regen is never read as an input surge\n  (LTC4364-1 would latch).\nR802/R803/R804 374k/15k/10k: UV 20 V, OV 50 V. D802/D803 15 V gate zeners (datasheet: required at >= 24 V).\n  SHDN and ENOUT unused.\nLATCH-OFF (-1): a fault kills every rail; D6 + R30 27k from VIN_RAW light on FLT with the board dark (FLT\n  sinks <= 2 mA: 1.3 mA at 36 V). Power-cycle to clear.\nQ1/Q2 PSMN3R7-100BSE: hot-swap SOA ~30 A at 36 V for 1 ms (25 C), 2.4x margin over the folded-back short. R2 =\n  INA228 shunt, WSK1216 true 4-terminal Kelvin."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 127 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8c2f64fc-b39e-4d7d-ab14-a4fe0fa67454")
	)
